+Surface: add a tail branch statement to contract source
+
+Add `if le a b then BODY else BODY` as the last statement of an entry
+body. Both legs are necessary, and each leg can end in a different
+tail branch. Lower it to the core `le` branch with the same bindings,
+state and proof evidence in each leg. Include leg statements in the
+contract step scans. Reserve `if`, `then` and `else`.
+
+Refuse a statement after the branch, a condition that is not `le`, a
+missing `else` and a branch in a constructor.
+
+Add a source example, a SURFACE-BRANCH gate leg under the new
+`--surface-branch` mode and four built mutations with controls. Keep
+`--m2-reconcile` at 110 legs. Raise the emitter line bound from 1800
+to 1815 and the ratified total from 3550 to 3565 (USER ruling
+2026-10-06). Update the `dev/DENOMINATORS.sha256` lines of `Makefile`,
+`dev/stage-a-gates.py` and `src/emitter.bend`.
