@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Surface branch mutations
+
+Each mutation is compiled in a disposable copy. The build must succeed.
+The named witness must exit 1 with its diagnostic. The restored source
+must rebuild and pass the same witness.
+
+| Mutation | Changed behavior | Witness |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| LEGS | Lower the branch with the THEN and ELSE legs exchanged | Five-file comparison with the `guard` program |
+| OPERANDS | Lower `le a b` as `le b a` | Five-file comparison with the `guard` program |
+| TAIL | Accept a statement after the `if` | Refuse a statement after the `if` |
+| SCAN | Omit leg statements from the contract step scans | Caller read and ABI state mutability in a leg |
+
+LEGS and OPERANDS change `Local.Contract.lower.f12919` and fail
+`SURFACE-BRANCH-PAIR`. TAIL changes `Contract.branch` and fails
+`SURFACE-BRANCH-REFUSAL trailing`. SCAN changes `Contract.all_steps` and
+fails `SURFACE-BRANCH-SCAN`. `mutations/surface-branch.json` holds the
+four replacements and a SHA-256 for each replaced definition. The test
+saves the exit codes, markers and source hashes as `MUTANTS`.
+
+Status: the mutations have not run. See the
+[slice notes](SURFACE-BRANCH.md).
