@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Contract surface branch
+
+This slice starts at `30feb7b02baa1964e0743aedfb0d4b477c9b870a`. It is
+not part of an M1 or M2 milestone group. It adds one statement to
+contract source:
+
+```text
+entry settle (bonus : Word) : Eff Sig Word := do
+  d <- sload verdict ;
+  if le d (word 1) then
+    pure (word 1)
+  else
+    revert
+```
+
+`if le a b then BODY else BODY` must be the last statement of an entry
+body. Both legs are necessary. Each leg is a statement list with its
+own ending, which can be a different tail `if`. The statement lowers to
+the [core](M1-SURFACE.md) `le a b THEN ELSE`, which runs THEN when
+`a <= b` as unsigned Words. Each leg lowers with the bindings, state,
+written fields and proof evidence of the statements before the `if`.
+Literal operands use `(word N)`.
+
+The two contract-wide step scans include the statements in both legs.
+Thus effect selection and ABI state mutability see a read or a write
+that occurs only in a leg. `if`, `then` and `else` are reserved source
+names.
+
+The parser refuses these sources:
+
+| Source | Code |
+| --- | --- |
+| A statement after the `if`, at the top or in a leg | `SURFACE_BRANCH` |
+| A condition that is not `le a b` | `SURFACE_BRANCH` |
+| An `if` in a constructor | `SURFACE_BRANCH` |
+| An `if` without `else` | `SURFACE_SYNTAX` |
+| A leg that uses a name that is not in its scope | `SURFACE_SCOPE` |
+| A field or a binding named `else` or `then` | `SURFACE_NAME` |
+
+The kernel, core recognizer, model and axiom set do not change. No new
+axiom or runtime intrinsic is added. Programs that do not use the three
+reserved names keep their artifacts.
+
+[SurfaceBranch.asy](../examples/SurfaceBranch.asy) has a three-way
+nested `settle` on plain Word fields:
+
+```sh
+_build/bin/assay emit examples/SurfaceBranch.asy -o SurfaceBranch-out
+python3 -P dev/surface-branch-test.py
+python3 -P dev/stage-a-gates.py --surface-branch
+```
+
+The focused gate has five parts. `live` runs 30 cases (three bonus
+values, five verdicts and two callers) and compares the source model
+and geth with independent expectations. `pairs` compares all five
+emitted files of `if .. else revert` with the equivalent `guard`
+program, also in a nested leg. `scan` checks a caller read that occurs
+only in a leg and the ABI state mutability. `refusals` checks eight
+invalid sources. `mutants` builds the four
+[mutations](SURFACE-BRANCH-MUTATIONS.md) with restored controls.
+
+`--surface-branch` runs the 110 `--m2-reconcile` legs and then
+SURFACE-BRANCH, for 111 legs. `--m2-reconcile` and its record do not
+change.
+
+The emitter measures 1812/1815 lines. USER ruling 2026-10-06 raises the
+emitter bound in `dev/trusted-lines.py` from 1800 to 1815 and the
+ratified total from 3550 to 3565.
+
+Status: `live`, `pairs`, `scan` and `refusals` pass. The mutants and
+the full gate have not run. They wait until the M2 closure battery
+ends, to keep load off that run.
